        <mxCell id="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-21" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Create a basic solution design&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Create a detailed solution design&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Source/develop/configure the components&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Source/build/configure the solution&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Support validation and testing&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Support deployment and release&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Review solution development and implementation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the infrastructure and platform management practice is to oversee the infrastructure and platforms used by an organization. When carried out properly, this practice enables the monitoring of technology solutions available to the organization, including the technology and external service providers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to establish a solid approach for releasing the deliverables, in order to orderly introduce components in the IT architecture or the enterprise.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Infrastructure and Platform Management (3.2.3)&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-20" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
