        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-49" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Develop and agree the PPM approach&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Communicate and embed the PPM approach&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Review and adjust the PPM approach&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the project management practice is to ensure that all projects in the organization are successfully delivered. This is achieved by planning, delegating, monitoring, and maintaining control of all aspects of a project, and ensuring motivation for the people involved.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, want agile solution development projects to follow the organization&#39;s approach to program and project management, in order to follow an organization-wide homogeneous approach or at least remain within the set boundaries.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: Project management (3.2.2)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-48" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-50" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Project&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;management (3.2.2)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Directing projects" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4981.75" y="1638" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="4713" y="1990" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-51" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Authorize initiation&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Authorize a stage or exception plan&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Give ad hoc direction&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Authorize project closure&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the project management practice is to ensure that all projects in the organization are successfully delivered. This is achieved by planning, delegating, monitoring, and maintaining control of all aspects of a project, and ensuring motivation for the people involved.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to follow the organization&#39;s approach to direct projects, in order to follow an organization-wide homogeneous approach or at least remain within the set boundaries.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Project&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;management (3.2.3)&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-50" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-52" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;entryX=0;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitX=1;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" parent="1" source="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-48" target="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-50" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="4571.75" y="1648" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="4631.75" y="1648" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTJ3HsHo-e2HUiJ0V5Zs-5" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ISO 27001 &amp;amp; 27002 - 5.31&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Legal, statutory, regulatory and contractual requirements" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="5392.5" y="1642" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5430" y="3252" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTJ3HsHo-e2HUiJ0V5Zs-6" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Legal, statutory, regulatory and contractual requirements relevant to information security and the organization’s approach to meet these requirements should be identified, documented and kept up to date.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;To ensure compliance with legal, statutory, regulatory and contractual requirements related to information security.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to identify, document and update legal, statutory, regulatory and contractual requirements relevant for information security of the solution, in order to ensure compliance with those requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="oTJ3HsHo-e2HUiJ0V5Zs-5" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3NLvPx2ckS6_KmLze-8x-9" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ISO 27001 &amp;amp; 27002 - 8.25&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Secure development life cycle" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="5750" y="1639" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5427.5" y="4510" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3NLvPx2ckS6_KmLze-8x-10" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Rules for the secure development of software and systems should be established and applied.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;To ensure information security is designed and implemented within the secure development life cycle&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;of software and systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to follow the rules of the organization&#39;s secure development life cycle, in order to ensure information security information security is designed and implemented within the development phase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="3NLvPx2ckS6_KmLze-8x-9" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-5" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 14.5&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Train Workforce Members on Causes of Unintentional Data Exposure" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="6800" y="1641" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="6800" y="1641" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-6" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Train workforce members to be aware of causes for unintentional data exposure. Example topics include mis-delivery of sensitive data, losing a portable end-user device, or publishing data to unintended audiences.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;The actions of people play a critical part in the success or failure of an enterprise’s security program. It is easier for an attacker to entice a user to click a link or open an email attachment to install malware in order to get into an enterprise, than to find a network exploit to do it directly.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the organization, I want agile solution development projects to train project team members on data causes of unintentional data exposure, in order to increase knowledge and awareness on this vital security topic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-5" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-19" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 16.14&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Conduct Threat Modeling" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="7160" y="1641" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="7160" y="1641" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-20" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Conduct threat modeling. Threat modeling is the process of identifying and addressing application security design flaws within a design, before code is created. It is conducted through specially trained individuals who evaluate the application design and gauge security risks for each entry point and access level. The goal is to map out the application, architecture, and infrastructure in a structured way to understand its weaknesses.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Application vulnerabilities can be present for many reasons: insecure design, insecure infrastructure, coding mistakes, weak authentication, and failure to test for unusual or unexpected conditions.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the organization, I want agile solution development projects to assure the conduction of threat modelling, in order to identify and address application security design flaws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-19" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-31" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Organizational change management (3.2.1)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Organizational change lifecycle management" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4621.75" y="1548" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5073" y="1900" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-32" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Understand need and scope&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Create change team&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Create change vision, plan, quick wins&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Communicate change&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Lead to change, enable operation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Anchor new state of the system&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Sustain system&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the OCM practice is to ensure that changes in an organization are implemented smoothly and successfully, and that lasting benefits are achieved by managing the human aspects of the changes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, want agile solution development projects to identify the need for organisational change and work on a sustainable implementation, in order to transition the organization in a seamless and beneficial manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: Organizational change management (3.2.2)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-31" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-33" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Organizational change management&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;(3.2.2)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Management of change adaptive environment" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4981.75" y="1548" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5433" y="1900" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-34" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Understand internal organizational system&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Identify external factors and influences&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Optimize response&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Create adaptability improvement plan and initiate improvement within OCM&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the OCM practice is to ensure that changes in an organization are implemented smoothly and successfully, and that lasting benefits are achieved by managing the human aspects of the changes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to create a change adaptive environment, in order to establish an environment where change is part of the organizational culture.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-33" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-35" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;entryX=0;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitX=1;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" parent="1" source="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-31" target="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-33" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="4571.75" y="1558" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="4631.75" y="1558" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="iMIV0qhzkyAP3cC0WdMi-1" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ISO 27001 &amp;amp; 27002 - 5.23&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Information security for use of cloud services" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="5392.5" y="1550" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5430" y="8460" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="iMIV0qhzkyAP3cC0WdMi-2" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Processes for acquisition, use, management and exit from cloud services should be established in accordance with the organization’s information security requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;To specify and manage information security for the use of cloud services.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to familiarize themselves with the organizations topic-specific policy and processes on cloud services, in order to apply those requirements in case cloud resources are used.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="iMIV0qhzkyAP3cC0WdMi-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xloykYCow0mXDYhp3S2N-5" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ISO 27001 &amp;amp; 27002 - 7.7&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Clear desk and clear screen" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="5751.25" y="1549" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5428.75" y="4420" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xloykYCow0mXDYhp3S2N-6" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Clear desk rules for papers and removable storage media and clear screen rules for information&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;processing facilities should be defined and appropriately enforced.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;To reduce the risks of unauthorized access, loss of and damage to information on desks, screens and in&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;other accessible locations during and outside normal working hours.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to follow and enforce clear desk rules, in order to reduce the risk of unauthorized access, loss or damage to information.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="xloykYCow0mXDYhp3S2N-5" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-3" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 14.4&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Train Workforce on Data Handling Best Practices" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="6800" y="1549" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="6800" y="1549" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-4" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Train workforce members on how to identify and properly store, transfer, archive, and destroy sensitive data. This also includes training workforce members on clear screen and desk best practices, such as locking their screen when they step away from their enterprise asset, erasing physical and virtual whiteboards at the end of meetings, and storing data and assets securely.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;The actions of people play a critical part in the success or failure of an enterprise’s security program. It is easier for an attacker to entice a user to click a link or open an email attachment to install malware in order to get into an enterprise, than to find a network exploit to do it directly.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the organization, I want agile solution development projects to train project team members on data handling best practices, in order to increase knowledge and awareness on this vital security topic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-3" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-15" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 16.13&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Conduct Application Penetration Testing" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="7160" y="1548" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="7160" y="1548" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-16" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Conduct application penetration testing. For critical applications, authenticated penetration testing is better suited to finding business logic vulnerabilities than code scanning and automated security testing. Penetration testing relies on the skill of the tester to manually manipulate an application as an authenticated and unauthenticated user.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Application vulnerabilities can be present for many reasons: insecure design, insecure infrastructure, coding mistakes, weak authentication, and failure to test for unusual or unexpected conditions.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the organization, I want agile solution development projects to assure the conduction of application penetration tests for critical applications or components, in order to avoid business logic vulnerabilities and identify more sophisticated vulnerabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-15" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-13" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Measurement and reporting (3.2.1)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Designing the measurement and reporting system" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4981.75" y="1458" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5433" y="1810" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-14" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Developing metrics and measurement methods&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Forming KPI scorecards&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Designing report templates and reporting policy&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the measurement and reporting practice is to support good decision-making and continual improvement by decreasing the levels of uncertainty. This is achieved through the collection of relevant data on various managed objects and the valid assessment of this data in an appropriate context.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, want agile solution development projects to develop metrics and measurements to sufficiently inform and report to the management, in order to support decision-making on the project/product/service.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: Measurement and reporting (3.2.2)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-13" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-24" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ISO 27001 &amp;amp; 27002 - 5.8&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Information security in project management" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="5393" y="1460" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5430.5" y="3070" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-25" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Information security should be integrated into project management.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;To ensure information security risks related to projects and deliverables are effectively addressed in&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;project management throughout the project life cycle.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to integrate information security aspects in the management of projects, in order to address those risks in a very early stage and align the projects progress with the enterprise&#39;s operational processes and security requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-24" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xloykYCow0mXDYhp3S2N-3" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ISO 27001 &amp;amp; 27002 - 7.6&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Working in secure areas" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="5751.25" y="1459" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5428.75" y="4330" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="xloykYCow0mXDYhp3S2N-4" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Security measures for working in secure areas should be designed and implemented.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;To protect information and other associated assets in secure areas from damage and unauthorized&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;interference by personnel working in these areas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to follow or adapt security measures for working in secure areas, in order to protect information and other associated assets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="xloykYCow0mXDYhp3S2N-3" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-1" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 14.3&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Train Workforce Members on Authentication Best Practices" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="6800" y="1459" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="6800" y="1459" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-2" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Train workforce members on authentication best practices. Example topics include MFA, password composition, and credential management.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;The actions of people play a critical part in the success or failure of an enterprise’s security program. It is easier for an attacker to entice a user to click a link or open an email attachment to install malware in order to get into an enterprise, than to find a network exploit to do it directly.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management&amp;nbsp;the organization, I want agile solution development projects to train project team members on authentication best practices, in order to increase knowledge and awareness on this vital security topic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-7" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 16.9&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Train Developers in Application Security Concepts and Secure Coding" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="7160" y="1458" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="7160" y="1458" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-8" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Ensure that all software development personnel receive training in writing secure code for their specific development environment and responsibilities. Training can include general security principles and application security standard practices. Conduct training at least annually and design in a way to promote security within the development team, and build a culture of security among the developers.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Application vulnerabilities can be present for many reasons: insecure design, insecure infrastructure, coding mistakes, weak authentication, and failure to test for unusual or unexpected conditions.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the organization, I want agile solution development projects to assure that relevant project team members are trained on application security concepts and secure coding, in order to assure necessary competences in that field during their activities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-7" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-3" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Knowledge management (3.2.1)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Establishing and maintaining the knowledge management environment" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4621.75" y="1368" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="4713" y="1720" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-4" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Understand current culture of knowledge usage and knowledge sharing&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Review external and internal requirements and factors of influence&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Optimize response, identify improvements&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Promote and empower usage of knowledge management practice across the organization&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Review knowledge management practice application and initiate improvements&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the knowledge management practice is to maintain and improve the effective, efficient, and convenient use of information and knowledge across the organization.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, want agile solution development projects to contribute to a well established knowledge management environment, in order to maintain solution/product/project knowledge in a manner that fits to the enterprise.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: Knowledge management (3.2.2)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-3" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-5" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Knowledge management (3.2.2)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; On-demand information discovery" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4981.75" y="1368" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5073" y="1720" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-6" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Registration of information request&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Research and data collection&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Information processing and presentation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Information acceptance&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Knowledge integration and review&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the knowledge management practice is to maintain and improve the effective, efficient, and convenient use of information and knowledge across the organization.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to follow and apply on-demand information discovery processes to be established, in order to explore and research new information in an adequate quality.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Knowledge&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;management (3.2.3)&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-5" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-7" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;entryX=0;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitX=1;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" parent="1" source="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-3" target="nB1jEptSUxtJqMZ95UXG-5" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="4571.75" y="1378" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="4631.75" y="1378" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-18" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ISO 27001 &amp;amp; 27002 - 5.5&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Contact with authorities" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="5394.25" y="1370" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5431.75" y="2980" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-19" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The organization should establish and maintain contact with relevant authorities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;To ensure appropriate flow of information takes place with respect to information security between&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;the organization and relevant legal, regulatory and supervisory authorities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to evaluate the necessity for information exchange between the organization and authorities and initiate it if necessary, in order to maintain a good collaboration and address points of attention in an early stage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-18" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ZFYketriOgI-VsJBwGQb-11" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ISO 27001 &amp;amp; 27002 - 6.8&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Information security event reporting" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="5751.25" y="1369" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5428.75" y="4240" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ZFYketriOgI-VsJBwGQb-12" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The organization should provide a mechanism for personnel to report observed or suspected&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;information security events through appropriate channels in a timely manner.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;To support timely, consistent and effective reporting of information security events that can be&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;identified by personnel.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to assure that project personnel is informed about channels to report suspected information security events, in order to enable reacting to those events in a timely, consistent and effective manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="ZFYketriOgI-VsJBwGQb-11" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="kiCtRI2jYFqAnLlAU17V-73" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 14.2&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Train Workforce Members to Recognize Social Engineering Attacks" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="6800" y="1369" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="6800" y="1369" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="kiCtRI2jYFqAnLlAU17V-74" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Train workforce members to recognize social engineering attacks, such as phishing, business email compromise (BEC), pretexting, and tailgating.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;The actions of people play a critical part in the success or failure of an enterprise’s security program. It is easier for an attacker to entice a user to click a link or open an email attachment to install malware in order to get into an enterprise, than to find a network exploit to do it directly.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the organization, I want agile solution development projects to train project team members on how to identify social engineering attacks and provide specific scenarios in context of the developed solution to the organization, in order to increase the organization&#39;s ability to recognize social engineering attacks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="kiCtRI2jYFqAnLlAU17V-73" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-28" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 15.7&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Securely Decommission Service Providers" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="7160" y="1369" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="7160" y="1369" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-29" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Securely decommission service providers. Example considerations include user and service account deactivation, termination of data flows, and secure disposal of enterprise data within service provider systems.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;In our modern, connected world, enterprises rely on vendors and partners to help manage their data or rely on infrastructure for core applications or functions.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the organization, I want agile solution development projects to consider and develop exit plans for secure decommissioning of service providers used in the project, in order to avoid vender lock-ins.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-28" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-50" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 18.5&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Perform Periodic Internal Penetration Tests" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="7520" y="1368" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="7520" y="1368" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-51" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Perform periodic internal penetration tests based on program requirements, no less than annually. The testing may be clear box or opaque box.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Penetration testing starts with the reconnaissance of the enterprise and environment, and scanning to identify the vulnerabilities that can be used as entries into the enterprise.&amp;nbsp;Vulnerabilities will be identified in these targets. Exploits to these vulnerabilities are executed to demonstrate how an adversary would attack.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the organization, I want agile solution development projects to participate in periodic internal penetration tests if deemed necessary, in order to assure an adequate coverage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-50" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="BSoNbctEzULQwdFmj1DB-3" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Architecture management (3.2.1)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Architecture governance" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4621.75" y="1278" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5073" y="1630" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="BSoNbctEzULQwdFmj1DB-4" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Analyse the organization and requirements&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Develop and agree architecture vision&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Monitor the organization&#39;s architecture&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the architecture management practice is to explain the different elements that form an organization. This practice explains how the elements interrelate to enable the organization to effectively achieve its current and future objectives.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects follow the architectural vision, principles and requirements and update them where necessary, in order to maintain a coherent architecture vision, principles and requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: Architecture management (3.2.2)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="BSoNbctEzULQwdFmj1DB-3" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="BSoNbctEzULQwdFmj1DB-5" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Architecture management (3.2.2)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Development of a target architecture and road map" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4981.75" y="1278" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5433" y="1630" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="BSoNbctEzULQwdFmj1DB-6" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Identify requirements&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Document current architecture&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Develop target architecture&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Design standards, frameworks, and guidelines&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Design agree, and communicate architecture road map&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the architecture management practice is to explain the different elements that form an organization. This practice explains how the elements interrelate to enable the organization to effectively achieve its current and future objectives.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to be reflected in the current and target architecture model, adhere to architecture controls, frameworks and guidelines as well as be reflected in the architecture road map, in order to fit into to meet all architectural requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Architecture management (3.2.3)&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="BSoNbctEzULQwdFmj1DB-5" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="BSoNbctEzULQwdFmj1DB-7" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;entryX=0;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitX=1;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" parent="1" source="BSoNbctEzULQwdFmj1DB-3" target="BSoNbctEzULQwdFmj1DB-5" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="4571.75" y="1288" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="4631.75" y="1288" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-16" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ISO 27001 &amp;amp; 27002 - 5.4&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Management responsibilities" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="5393" y="1280" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5430.5" y="2890" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-17" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Management should require all personnel to apply information security in accordance with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;established information security policy, topic-specific policies and procedures of the organization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;To ensure management understand their role in information security and undertake actions aiming to&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;ensure all personnel are aware of and fulfil their information security responsibilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want all personnel of agile solution development projects to be apply information security in accordance with the company policy, in order to assure a consistent security governance and management.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-16" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ZFYketriOgI-VsJBwGQb-9" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ISO 27001 &amp;amp; 27002 - 6.7&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Remote working" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="5751.25" y="1279" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5428.75" y="4150" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ZFYketriOgI-VsJBwGQb-10" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Security measures should be implemented when personnel are working remotely to protect information&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;accessed, processed or stored outside the organization’s premises.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;To ensure the security of information when personnel are working remotely.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to assure that security measures are intact and followed when information is accessed, processed or stored outside the organization&#39;s premises, in order to protect information when working remotely.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="ZFYketriOgI-VsJBwGQb-9" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="kiCtRI2jYFqAnLlAU17V-71" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 14.1&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Establish and Maintain a Security Awareness Program" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="6800" y="1278" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="6800" y="1278" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="kiCtRI2jYFqAnLlAU17V-72" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Establish and maintain a security awareness program. The purpose of a security awareness program is to educate the enterprise’s workforce on how to interact with enterprise assets and data in a secure manner. Conduct training at hire and, at a minimum, annually. Review and update content annually, or when significant enterprise changes occur that could impact this Safeguard.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;The actions of people play a critical part in the success or failure of an enterprise’s security program. It is easier for an attacker to entice a user to click a link or open an email attachment to install malware in order to get into an enterprise, than to find a network exploit to do it directly.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the organization, I want agile solution development projects to onboard project team members to the organization&#39;s security awareness program, in order to raise their awareness on security aspects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="kiCtRI2jYFqAnLlAU17V-71" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-26" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 15.6&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Monitor Service Providers" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="7160" y="1279" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="7160" y="1279" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-27" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Monitor service providers consistent with the enterprise’s service provider management policy. Monitoring may include periodic reassessment of service provider compliance, monitoring service provider release notes, and dark web monitoring.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;In our modern, connected world, enterprises rely on vendors and partners to help manage their data or rely on infrastructure for core applications or functions.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the organization, I want agile solution development projects to onboard used service providers to the organization&#39;s monitoring process of service providers, in order to monitor them according to the organization&#39;s practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="ibRm7NSeTpzZEgZbGgji-26" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-43" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 18.2&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Perform Periodic External Penetration Tests" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="7520" y="1279" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="7520" y="1279" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-44" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Perform periodic external penetration tests based on program requirements, no less than annually. External penetration testing must include enterprise and environmental reconnaissance to detect exploitable information. Penetration testing requires specialized skills and experience and must be conducted through a qualified party. The testing may be clear box or opaque box.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Penetration testing starts with the reconnaissance of the enterprise and environment, and scanning to identify the vulnerabilities that can be used as entries into the enterprise.&amp;nbsp;Vulnerabilities will be identified in these targets. Exploits to these vulnerabilities are executed to demonstrate how an adversary would attack.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the organization, I want agile solution development projects to participate in periodic external penetration tests if deemed necessary, in order to assure an adequate coverage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-43" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-17" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 3.8&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Document Data Flows" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16420" y="6638" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="14210" y="6340" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-18" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Document data flows. Data flow documentation includes service provider data flows and should be based on the enterprise’s data management process. Review and update documentation annually, or when significant enterprise changes occur that could impact this Safeguard.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Data privacy has become increasingly important, and enterprises are learning that privacy is about the appropriate use and management of data, not just encryption. Data must be appropriately managed through its entire life cycle.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to document their data flows and update them regularly, in order to maintain oversight on processed data.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-17" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-15" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 3.7&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Establish and Maintain a Data Classification Scheme" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16421.25" y="6547.83" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="6720" y="3031" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-16" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Establish and maintain an overall data classification scheme for the enterprise. Enterprises may use labels, such as “Sensitive,” “Confidential,” and “Public,” and classify their data according to those labels. Review and update the classification scheme annually, or when significant enterprise changes occur that could impact this Safeguard.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Data privacy has become increasingly important, and enterprises are learning that privacy is about the appropriate use and management of data, not just encryption. Data must be appropriately managed through its entire life cycle.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to classify data according to the organization&#39;s scheme, in order to enable users and tools to understand the necessity of protection for the classified data.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-15" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-11" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 3.5&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Securely Dispose of Data" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16420" y="6458" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="14210" y="6160" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-12" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Securely dispose of data as outlined in the enterprise’s documented data management process. Ensure the disposal process and method are commensurate with the data sensitivity.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Data privacy has become increasingly important, and enterprises are learning that privacy is about the appropriate use and management of data, not just encryption. Data must be appropriately managed through its entire life cycle.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to define data disposal requirements and ensure operational data disposal, in order securely delete all data that is not needed anymore.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-11" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-9" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 3.4&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Enforce Data Retention" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16420" y="6368" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="6720" y="5481" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-10" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Retain data according to the enterprise’s documented data management process. Data retention must include both minimum and maximum timelines.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Data privacy has become increasingly important, and enterprises are learning that privacy is about the appropriate use and management of data, not just encryption. Data must be appropriately managed through its entire life cycle.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to define data retention requirements and enforce operational data retention, in order retain all necessary data.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-9" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-3" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 3.2&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Establish and Maintain a Data Inventory" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16420" y="6278" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="14210" y="5980" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-4" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Establish and maintain a data inventory based on the enterprise’s data management process. Inventory sensitive data, at a minimum. Review and update inventory annually, at a minimum, with a priority on sensitive data.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Data privacy has become increasingly important, and enterprises are learning that privacy is about the appropriate use and management of data, not just encryption. Data must be appropriately managed through its entire life cycle.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to maintain the information of the data processed in the data inventory, in order maintain oversight of the processed data.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="INdrnmeXtqBlZBc4LRKb-3" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pFyAgszVoUyKk6v15XwR-4" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 3.1&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Establish and Maintain a Data Management Process" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16420" y="6188" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="7384.25" y="2951" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pFyAgszVoUyKk6v15XwR-5" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Establish and maintain a documented data management process. In the process, address data sensitivity, data owner, handling of data, data retention limits, and disposal requirements, based on sensitivity and retention standards for the enterprise. Review and update documentation annually, or when significant enterprise changes occur that could impact this Safeguard.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Data privacy has become increasingly important, and enterprises are learning that privacy is about the appropriate use and management of data, not just encryption. Data must be appropriately managed through its entire life cycle.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to participate in the data management process and meet its requirements, in order maintain oversight of the processed data.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="pFyAgszVoUyKk6v15XwR-4" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-29" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 2.7&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Allowlist Authorized Scripts" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16420" y="6098" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5427.5" y="12420" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-30" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Use technical controls, such as digital signatures and version control, to ensure that only authorized scripts, such as specific .ps1, and .py files are allowed to execute. Block unauthorized scripts from executing. Reassess bi-annually, or more frequently.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;A complete software inventory is a critical foundation for preventing attacks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;For example, if a user opens a malicious website or attachment with a vulnerable browser, an attacker can often install backdoor programs and bots that give the attacker long-term control of the system. W&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;ithout a complete inventory of software assets, an enterprise cannot determine if they have vulnerable software, or if there are potential licensing violations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to assure that necessary scripts are on the allowlist, assure that tools blocking scripts are installed and information is provided to reassessment process, in order to keep the technical control for preventing unauthorized scripts effective.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-29" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-27" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 2.6&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Allowlist Authorized Libraries" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16420" y="6008" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5427.5" y="12330" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-28" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Use technical controls to ensure that only authorized software libraries, such as specific .dll, .ocx, and .so files, are allowed to load into a system process. Block unauthorized libraries from loading into a system process. Reassess bi-annually, or more frequently.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;A complete software inventory is a critical foundation for preventing attacks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;For example, if a user opens a malicious website or attachment with a vulnerable browser, an attacker can often install backdoor programs and bots that give the attacker long-term control of the system. W&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;ithout a complete inventory of software assets, an enterprise cannot determine if they have vulnerable software, or if there are potential licensing violations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to assure that necessary libraries are on the allowlist, assure that tools blocking libraries are installed and information is provided to reassessment process, in order to keep the technical control for preventing unauthorized libraries effective.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-27" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-25" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 2.5&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Allowlist Authorized Software" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16420" y="5918" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5427.5" y="12240" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-26" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Use technical controls, such as application allowlisting, to ensure that only authorized software can execute or be accessed. Reassess bi-annually, or more frequently.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;A complete software inventory is a critical foundation for preventing attacks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;For example, if a user opens a malicious website or attachment with a vulnerable browser, an attacker can often install backdoor programs and bots that give the attacker long-term control of the system. W&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;ithout a complete inventory of software assets, an enterprise cannot determine if they have vulnerable software, or if there are potential licensing violations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to assure that necessary applications are on the allowlist, assure that tools blocking software are installed and information is provided to reassessment process, in order to keep the technical control for preventing unauthorized software effective.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-25" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-36" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 17.8&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Conduct Post-Incident Reviews" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16781.25" y="5918" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="15331.25" y="5580" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-37" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Conduct post-incident reviews. Post-incident reviews help prevent incident recurrence through identifying lessons learned and follow-up action.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Administrative, or highly privileged, accounts are a particular target, because they allow attackers to add other accounts, or make changes to assets that could make them more vulnerable to other attacks.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to participate in post-incident reviews, in order to prevent incident reccurence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="j14fxGzRAlY_bbs1dScx-36" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-23" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 2.4&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Utilize Automated Software Inventory Tools" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16421.25" y="5828" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5428.75" y="12150" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-24" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Utilize software inventory tools, when possible, throughout the enterprise to automate the discovery and documentation of installed software.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;A complete software inventory is a critical foundation for preventing attacks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;For example, if a user opens a malicious website or attachment with a vulnerable browser, an attacker can often install backdoor programs and bots that give the attacker long-term control of the system. W&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;ithout a complete inventory of software assets, an enterprise cannot determine if they have vulnerable software, or if there are potential licensing violations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to enable automated software inventory tools to scan the projects system parameter and infrastructure components, in order to have just authorized software in use within the organization.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-23" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-11" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 5.6&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Centralize Account Management" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16780" y="5828" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="13610" y="6660" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-12" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Centralize account management through a directory or identity service.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Administrative, or highly privileged, accounts are a particular target, because they allow attackers to add other accounts, or make changes to assets that could make them more vulnerable to other attacks.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to assure that all accounts are onboarded onto a centralize account management, in order to maintain an organization-wide overview.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-11" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-21" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 2.3&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Address Unauthorized Software" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16421.25" y="5738" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5428.75" y="12060" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-22" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Ensure that unauthorized software is either removed from use on enterprise assets or receives a documented exception. Review monthly, or more frequently.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;A complete software inventory is a critical foundation for preventing attacks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;For example, if a user opens a malicious website or attachment with a vulnerable browser, an attacker can often install backdoor programs and bots that give the attacker long-term control of the system. W&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;ithout a complete inventory of software assets, an enterprise cannot determine if they have vulnerable software, or if there are potential licensing violations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to address and potentially remove unauthorized software on the systems in scope of the project, in order to have just authorized software in use within the organization.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-21" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-9" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 5.5&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Establish and Maintain an Inventory of Service Accounts" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16780" y="5738" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="13610" y="6570" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-10" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Establish and maintain an inventory of service accounts. The inventory, at a minimum, must contain department owner, review date, and purpose. Perform service account reviews to validate that all active accounts are authorized, on a recurring schedule at a minimum quarterly, or more frequently.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Administrative, or highly privileged, accounts are a particular target, because they allow attackers to add other accounts, or make changes to assets that could make them more vulnerable to other attacks.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to keep the information in the inventory of service accounts up-to-date, in order to maintain a sufficient overview.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-9" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-19" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 2.2&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Ensure Authorized Software is Currently Supported" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16421.25" y="5648" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5428.75" y="11970" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-20" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Ensure that only currently supported software is designated as authorized in the software inventory for enterprise assets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;A complete software inventory is a critical foundation for preventing attacks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;For example, if a user opens a malicious website or attachment with a vulnerable browser, an attacker can often install backdoor programs and bots that give the attacker long-term control of the system. W&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;ithout a complete inventory of software assets, an enterprise cannot determine if they have vulnerable software, or if there are potential licensing violations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to assure that just currently supported software is used and that they support security functions in their efforts to address unauthorized software, in order to have just supported software in use within the organization.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-19" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-3" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 5.2&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Use Unique Passwords" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16780" y="5648" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="13610" y="6480" width="360" height="411" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-4" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Use unique passwords for all enterprise assets. Best practice implementation includes, at a minimum, an 8-character password for accounts using Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) and a 14-character password for accounts not using MFA.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Administrative, or highly privileged, accounts are a particular target, because they allow attackers to add other accounts, or make changes to assets that could make them more vulnerable to other attacks.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to use strong passwords and review their used passwords before releasing any feature, in order to avoid going in production with weakly protected accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-3" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-17" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 2.1&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Establish and Maintain a Software Inventory" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16424.25" y="5558" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5431.75" y="11880" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-18" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Establish and maintain a detailed inventory of all licensed software installed on enterprise assets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;A complete software inventory is a critical foundation for preventing attacks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;For example, if a user opens a malicious website or attachment with a vulnerable browser, an attacker can often install backdoor programs and bots that give the attacker long-term control of the system. W&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;ithout a complete inventory of software assets, an enterprise cannot determine if they have vulnerable software, or if there are potential licensing violations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to maintain the information in the software inventory, in order to enable security functions to keep an overview.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="UZmQJI8PMWxO6t6RksVb-17" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-1" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;CIS CSC - 5.1&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Establish and Maintain an Inventory of Accounts" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="16780" y="5558" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="13610" y="6390" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-2" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Establish and maintain an inventory of all accounts managed in the enterprise. The inventory must at a minimum include user, administrator accounts, and service accounts. The inventory, at a minimum, should contain the person’s name, username, start/stop dates, and department. Validate that all active accounts are authorized, on a recurring schedule at a minimum quarterly, or more frequently.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Administrative, or highly privileged, accounts are a particular target, because they allow attackers to add other accounts, or make changes to assets that could make them more vulnerable to other attacks.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to keep the information in the inventory of accounts up-to-date, in order to maintain a sufficient overview.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="a5HJ6gRi5xYlhZZS6_cq-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-26" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ISO 27001 &amp;amp; 27002 - 5.9&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Inventory of information and other associated assets" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="15030" y="5598" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5431.25" y="12540" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-27" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;An inventory of information and other associated assets, including owners, should be developed and&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;maintained.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;To identify the organization’s information and other associated assets in order to preserve their&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;information security and assign appropriate ownership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to identify and register all information and other associated assets already during the development phase, in order to enable an adequate protection of information and assets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="bgYUZ9FqRBf7vEnh27Lf-26" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-15" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 - Deployment Management&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;(3.2.2)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Deployment models development and review" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="13650" y="5849" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5433" y="6360" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-16" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Deployment model planning&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Deployment model implementation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Deployment model testing&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Deployment review and deployment records analysis&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Deployment model improvement initiation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Deployment model update and communication&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the deployment management practice is to move new or changed hardware, software, documentation, processes, or any other component to live environments. It may also be involved in deploying components to other environments for testing or staging.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to continuously improve the deployment model, in order to adapt it in a manner that it meets the enterprises requrirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-15" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="x0tNCmZjMzLHtTbmIZVQ-11" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Service configuration&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;management (3.2.2)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Capturing, managing, and providing configuration information" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="13650" y="5759" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5070.5" y="2620" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="x0tNCmZjMzLHtTbmIZVQ-12" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Analyse resources and identify CIs&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Confirm a CI model&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Follow the CI model&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Manage exceptions&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Review the CI model&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the service configuration management practice is to ensure that accurate and reliable information about the configuration of services, and the configuration items that support them, is available when and where it is needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to keep the configuration information current, in order to assure that all service management processes have up-to-date information.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Service configuration&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;management (3.2.3)&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="x0tNCmZjMzLHtTbmIZVQ-11" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="x0tNCmZjMzLHtTbmIZVQ-13" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Service configuration&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;management (3.2.3)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Verifying configuration data" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="14010" y="5759" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5430.5" y="2620" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="x0tNCmZjMzLHtTbmIZVQ-14" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Identify a CI model&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Verify configuration data&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Review the verification output&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Define and implement corrective actions&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Compose and communicate a CMDB verification report&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the service configuration management practice is to ensure that accurate and reliable information about the configuration of services, and the configuration items that support them, is available when and where it is needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects the be aware that verification are on-going or even have to be performed by them, in order to assure accurate information within the CMDB.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="x0tNCmZjMzLHtTbmIZVQ-13" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nVK2YNMN3wv4ctxS4OYY-7" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Service financial&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;management (3.2.3)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Management accounting" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="13650" y="5669" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5430.5" y="2270" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nVK2YNMN3wv4ctxS4OYY-8" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Identify and capture costs&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Select a cost allocation model&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Follow the cost allocation model&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Manage exceptions&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Provide standard and tailored reports&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the service financial management practice is to support the organization&#39;s strategies and plans for service management by ensuring that the organization&#39;s financial resources and investments are being used effectively.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to allocate and report costs correctly, in order to assure cost transparency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="nVK2YNMN3wv4ctxS4OYY-7" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="GwzLfTZYDkI80HiPmpim-4" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Information security management (3.2.1)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Security incident management" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="13650" y="5579" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="6578.75" y="5440" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="GwzLfTZYDkI80HiPmpim-5" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Preparation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Detection and reporting&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Triage and analysis&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Containment and recovery&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Post-incident activity&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the information security management practice is to protect the information needed by the organization to conduct its business.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to prepare and anticipate future security incidents, in order to keep the response time as short as possible.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: Security incident management (3.2.2)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="GwzLfTZYDkI80HiPmpim-4" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="QuHqFJcRldl6wBvhqh9c-4" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;COBIT 2019 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;BAI10.03&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Maintain and control configuration items." style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="11930" y="5909" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="4710" y="3650" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="QuHqFJcRldl6wBvhqh9c-5" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Maintain an up-to-date repository of configuration items (CIs) by&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;populating any configuration changes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Provide sufficient information about service assets to enable the service to be effectively managed. Assess the impact of changes and deal with service incidents.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want an up-to-date configuration management, in order to maintain an overview on the enterprise&#39;s configuration and maintain a valuable information source for other service processes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: BAI10.04&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="QuHqFJcRldl6wBvhqh9c-4" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-176" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;COBIT 2019 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;BAI09.04&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Optimize asset value." style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="11930" y="5819" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5070" y="3650" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-177" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Regularly review the overall asset base to identify ways to optimize value in alignment with business needs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Account for all I&amp;amp;T assets and optimize the value provided by their use.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to regularly review the IT assets of the project, in order to optimize value in alignment with business needs and not to lose oversight due to explorations or the evaluation of concepts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: BAI09.05&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-176" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-180" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;COBIT 2019 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;BAI09.05&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Manage licenses." style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="12290" y="5819" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5430" y="3650" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-181" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Manage software licenses to maintain the optimal number of licenses and support business requirements. Ensure that the number of licenses owned is sufficient to cover the installed software in use.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Account for all I&amp;amp;T assets and optimize the value provided by their use.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to maintain a sufficient number of licenses for the software in use, in order to work in a cost-efficient manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-180" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-182" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;entryX=0;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitX=1;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" parent="1" source="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-176" target="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-180" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="10752.5" y="6639" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="10812.5" y="6639" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-145" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;entryX=0;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitX=1;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" parent="1" source="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-148" target="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-146" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="12240" y="5739" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="12300" y="5739" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-146" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;COBIT 2019 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;BAI07.07&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Provide early production support." style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="12650" y="5729" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5070" y="4790" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-147" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;For an agreed period of time, provide early support to users and I&amp;amp;T operations to resolve issues and help stabilize the new solution.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Implement solutions safely and in line with the agreed expectations and outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want an early support to be provided to users and IT operations, in order to address issues early and stabilize new solutions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: BAI07.08&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-146" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-148" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;COBIT 2019 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;BAI07.06&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Promote to production and manage releases." style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="12290" y="5729" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="4710" y="4790" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-149" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Promote the accepted solution to the business and operations. Where appropriate, run the solution as a pilot implementation or in parallel with the old solution for a defined period and compare behavior and results. If significant problems occur, revert to the original environment based on the fallback/back-up plan. Manage releases of solution components.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Implement solutions safely and in line with the agreed expectations and outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want the release of new changes and the promotion to production to be well managed and organized, in order to reduce the risk and adverse effects on the business.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: BAI07.07&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-148" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-150" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;COBIT 2019 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;BAI07.08&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Perform a post-implementation review." style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="13010" y="5729" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5430" y="4790" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-151" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Conduct a post-implementation review to confirm outcome and results, identify lessons learned, and develop an action plan. Evaluate actual performance and outcomes of the new or changed service against expected performance and outcomes anticipated by the user or customer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Implement solutions safely and in line with the agreed expectations and outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want implementation to be reviewed in a post-implementation phase, in order to enable an enterprise to learn.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-150" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-152" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;entryX=0;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitX=1;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" parent="1" source="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-146" target="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-150" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="12950" y="5729" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="13010" y="5729" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-153" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;COBIT 2019 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;BAI07.05&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Perform acceptance tests." style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="11930" y="5729" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="4350" y="4790" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-154" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Test changes independently, in accordance with the defined test plan, prior to migration to the live operational environment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Implement solutions safely and in line with the agreed expectations and outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want IT changes to be tested according to the test plan prior to migration to the operational environment, in order to identify defects as early as possible and be able to address them without causing a quality reduction of operational services.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: BAI07.06&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-153" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-155" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;entryX=0;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitX=1;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" parent="1" source="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-153" target="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-148" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="11880.5" y="5739" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="11940.5" y="5739" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-126" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;COBIT 2019 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;BAI06.04&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;  Close and document the changes." style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="11930" y="5639" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="5430" y="4700" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-127" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Whenever changes are implemented, update the solution, user&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;documentation and procedures affected by the change.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Create optimal solutions that meet enterprise needs while minimizing risk.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to update the solution as well as documentation and procedures affected by the change, in order to assure a stable IT operation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="5n0gASPAGLLi4WL7JSeG-126" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-8" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Service Validation and Testing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;(3.2.2)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Service validation" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="13710" y="3908" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="6910.5" y="4610" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-9" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Documenting acceptance criteria&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Verifying acceptance criteria&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the service validation and testing practice is to ensure that new or changed products and services meet defined requirements. The definition of service value is based on input from customers, business objectives, and regulatory requirements and is documented as part of the design and transition value chain activity. These inputs are used to establish measurable quality and performance indicators that support the definition of assurance criteria and testing requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to contribute in developing acceptance criteria, in order to make it quantifiable when a service meets the quality criteria.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Service Validation and Testing (3.2.3)&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-8" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-10" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Service Validation and Testing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;(3.2.3)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Performing a test" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;startSize=60;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#A680B8;" parent="1" vertex="1" collapsed="1">
          <mxGeometry x="14070" y="3908" width="300" height="60" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle x="7270.5" y="4610" width="360" height="410" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-11" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Test planning and preparation&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Test execution&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Test exit criteria evaluation and reporting&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Test closure&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the service validation and testing practice is to ensure that new or changed products and services meet defined requirements. The definition of service value is based on input from customers, business objectives, and regulatory requirements and is documented as part of the design and transition value chain activity. These inputs are used to establish measurable quality and performance indicators that support the definition of assurance criteria and testing requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to contribute in performing the test of services, in order to enable testing of services supported by the project&#39;s developed solution.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-10" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="DO11c-6wLbNFiMZy8dLW-3" value="&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;ITIL 4 - Service Request M&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color); font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-family: monospace; font-size: 0px; font-style: normal; text-wrap: nowrap;&quot;&gt;GraphModel%3E%3Croot%3E%3CmxCell%20id%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3CmxCell%20id%3D%221%22%20parent%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3CmxCell%20id%3D%222%22%20value%3D%22%26amp%3Bnbsp%3B%20%26amp%3Bnbsp%3B%20%26amp%3Bnbsp%3B%20%26lt%3Bspan%20style%3D%26quot%3Bfont-weight%3A%20400%3B%26quot%3B%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bi%26gt%3BITIL%204%20-%26amp%3Bnbsp%3B%26lt%3B%2Fi%26gt%3B%26lt%3B%2Fspan%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bi%20style%3D%26quot%3Bborder-color%3A%20var(--border-color)%3B%20font-weight%3A%20400%3B%26quot%3B%26gt%3BKnowledge%20management%20(3.2.1)%26lt%3B%2Fi%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bbr%26gt%3B%26amp%3Bnbsp%3B%20%26amp%3Bnbsp%3B%20%26amp%3Bnbsp%3B%20%20Establishing%20and%20maintaining%20the%20knowledge%20management%20environment%22%20style%3D%22swimlane%3BwhiteSpace%3Dwrap%3Bhtml%3D1%3Balign%3Dleft%3BstartSize%3D60%3BfillColor%3D%23E1D5E7%3BstrokeColor%3D%23A680B8%3B%22%20vertex%3D%221%22%20collapsed%3D%221%22%20parent%3D%221%22%3E%3CmxGeometry%20x%3D%225073%22%20y%3D%221990%22%20width%3D%22300%22%20height%3D%2260%22%20as%3D%22geometry%22%3E%3CmxRectangle%20x%3D%224713%22%20y%3D%221720%22%20width%3D%22360%22%20height%3D%22410%22%20as%3D%22alternateBounds%22%2F%3E%3C%2FmxGeometry%3E%3C%2FmxCell%3E%3CmxCell%20id%3D%223%22%20value%3D%22%26lt%3Bb%26gt%3BControl%20Description%3A%26lt%3Bbr%26gt%3B%26lt%3B%2Fb%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bdiv%26gt%3B%26lt%3B%2Fdiv%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bdiv%26gt%3B-%20Understand%20current%20culture%20of%20knowledge%20usage%20and%20knowledge%20sharing%26lt%3B%2Fdiv%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bdiv%26gt%3B-%20Review%20external%20and%20internal%20requirements%20and%20factors%20of%20influence%26lt%3B%2Fdiv%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bdiv%26gt%3B-%20Optimize%20response%2C%20identify%20improvements%26lt%3B%2Fdiv%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bdiv%26gt%3B-%20Promote%20and%20empower%20usage%20of%20knowledge%20management%20practice%20across%20the%20organization%26lt%3B%2Fdiv%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bdiv%26gt%3B-%20Review%20knowledge%20management%20practice%20application%20and%20initiate%20improvements%26lt%3B%2Fdiv%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bdiv%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bbr%26gt%3B%26lt%3B%2Fdiv%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bb%26gt%3BControl%20Objective%3A%26lt%3Bbr%26gt%3B%26lt%3B%2Fb%26gt%3BThe%20purpose%20of%20the%20knowledge%20management%20practice%20is%20to%20maintain%20and%20improve%20the%20effective%2C%20efficient%2C%20and%20convenient%20use%20of%20information%20and%20knowledge%20across%20the%20organization.%26lt%3Bbr%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bspan%20style%3D%26quot%3Bborder-color%3A%20var(--border-color)%3B%20background-color%3A%20initial%3B%26quot%3B%26gt%3B%26lt%3B%2Fspan%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bbr%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bb%26gt%3BEnabler%20Story%3A%26lt%3B%2Fb%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bbr%26gt%3BAs%20management%20of%20the%20enterprise%2C%20want%20agile%20solution%20development%20projects%20to%20contribute%20to%20a%20well%20established%20knowledge%20management%20environment%2C%20in%20order%20to%20maintain%20solution%2Fproduct%2Fproject%20knowledge%20in%20a%20manner%20that%20fits%20to%20the%20enterprise.%26lt%3Bbr%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bbr%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bfont%20style%3D%26quot%3Bfont-size%3A%2010px%3B%26quot%3B%26gt%3B%26lt%3Bu%20style%3D%26quot%3Bborder-color%3A%20var(--border-color)%3B%26quot%3B%26gt%3BDirect%20Successor%26lt%3B%2Fu%26gt%3B%3A%20Knowledge%20management%20(3.2.2)%26lt%3B%2Ffont%26gt%3B%22%20style%3D%22rounded%3D0%3BwhiteSpace%3Dwrap%3Bhtml%3D1%3Balign%3Dleft%3BverticalAlign%3Dtop%3B%22%20vertex%3D%221%22%20parent%3D%222%22%3E%3CmxGeometry%20y%3D%2260%22%20width%3D%22360%22%20height%3D%22350%22%20as%3D%22geometry%22%2F%3E%3C%2FmxCell%3E%3CmxCell%20id%3D%224%22%20value%3D%22%26amp%3Bnbsp%3B%20%26amp%3Bnbsp%3B%20%26amp%3Bnbsp%3B%26amp%