        <mxCell id="FzpiOMwNagBz9-rqdHPx-10" value="&lt;b&gt;Control Description:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Customer and user satisfaction surveys&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Ongoing service quality monitoring&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Service review&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Service quality reporting&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Control Objective:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;The purpose of the service level management practice is to set clear business-based targets for service levels, and to ensure that delivery of services is properly assed, monitored, and managed against these targets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enabler Story:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;As management of the enterprise, I want agile solution development projects to maintain an oversight of service levels and service quality of their service providers, in order to assure an adequate provided service.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;border-color: var(--border-color);&quot;&gt;Direct Successor&lt;/u&gt;: None&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="FzpiOMwNagBz9-rqdHPx-9" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="60" width="360" height="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
